Subject: [PATCH] canvas: pixels written with putImageData read back as written

The fingerprint checker draws a path and text, writes a 64x64 palette with
putImageData and reads it back: about 9,000 bytes came back changed, where
stock Chrome gives 0. Every pixel of a random palette is unlike its
neighbours, so the noise moved each one, and the canvas counted as drawn
because of the earlier path and text.

A 2D context now keeps the region putImageData wrote since its last draw.
getImageData, toDataURL, toBlob and convertToBlob leave those pixels as
the canvas holds them; they still key the noise of their neighbours. Any
draw (fill, stroke, text, image, gradient) ends the region, and a reset,
a whole-canvas clear and a whole-canvas putImageData empty it. An exact
opaque fillRect keeps it, as it keeps the canvas undrawn. Structured
clones of an ImageBitmap cut from the canvas keep the old rule.

